<title>USA: Richmond Fed - service sector growth slows in May.</title>
<headline>Richmond Fed - service sector growth slows in May.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond indexes monitoring manufacturing and service-sector activity.</p>
<p> MANUFACTURING SURVEY     May    April</p>
<p>  Shipments		    21     15</p>
<p>  New Orders		   16     25</p>
<p>  Backlog Orders	     -6     10</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	11	1</p>
<p>  Average Workweek	    4	7</p>
<p>  Prices Received	  0.61   0.49</p>
<p>  Prices Paid	     -0.37   0.37</p>
<p> SERVICES SURVEY	    May    April</p>
<p>  Service Revenues	   26     33</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	19     11</p>
<p>  Service Wage		 26     26</p>
<p>  Retail Revenues	    14     36</p>
<p>  Retail Employees	    4	7</p>
<p>  Retail Wage		  25     23</p>
<p>  Shopper Traffic	    19     35</p>
<p>Note -- Each index equals the percentage of responding firms reporting increases minus the percentage reporting decreases. Prices received and prices paid are in response to the question &quot;What do you believe was the percentage price change in your industry on an annualized basis?&quot;</p>
<p>Results of the May manufacturing survey are based on responses from 81 of 178 firms queried. Results of the May service-sector survey are based on responses from 75 of 121 firms.</p>
</text>
